        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b3e21f92-fc06-5723-84ba-1a08b1a016f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carolina, Puerto Rico; San Juan; Montrose; Colorado\n- Organizations: Pro-Air Services\n- Airports: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport; Montrose Regional Airport\n- Topics: airport identifiers; airport type; location\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport has the identifiers IATA SJU, ICAO TJSJ, and FAA LID SJU.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is a joint civil-military international airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor and is also known as Isla Verde International Airport.\n- Montrose Regional Airport has the identifiers IATA MTJ, ICAO KMTJ, and FAA LID MTJ.\n- Montrose Regional Airport is a non-towered public airport on the northwest side of Montrose in zip code 81401 in southwestern Colorado.\n- Pro-Air Services is an air charter operator based at Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport in San Juan, Puerto Rico.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
